From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:07:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: firmware: google,gs101-acpm-ipc: allow assigned
 clocks

The bootloader leaves ACPM's DVFS domains at fixed rates (the memory bus
at 2028 MHz on the Pixel 6 Pro) and nothing in Linux scales them yet. Let
a board set a domain's rate at boot with assigned-clocks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml           | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml
index 908037b6b..3594fb906 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml
@@ -36,6 +36,13 @@ properties:
       appropriately with the clock scaling. The argument is the ID of the
       clock contained by the firmware messages.
 
+  assigned-clocks:
+    description:
+      Firmware clocks to set at boot, for a board whose bootloader leaves
+      a domain at a rate nothing else scales yet.
+
+  assigned-clock-rates: true
+
   mboxes:
     maxItems: 1
 
